#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:3
msgid "Testing the GPU C library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:6
msgid ""
"Running GPU tests with high parallelism is likely to cause spurious "
"failures, out of resource errors, or indefinite hangs. limiting the number "
"of threads used while testing using `LIBC_GPU_TEST_JOBS=<N>` is highly "
"recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:11
msgid "Testing infrastructure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:13
msgid ""
"The LLVM C library supports different kinds of {ref}`tests <build_and_test>` "
"depending on the build configuration. The GPU target is considered a full "
"build and therefore provides all of its own utilities to build and run the "
"generated tests. Currently the GPU supports two kinds of tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:18
msgid ""
"**Hermetic tests** - These are unit tests built with a test suite similar to "
"Google's `gtest` infrastructure. These use the same infrastructure as unit "
"tests except that the entire environment is self-hosted. This allows us to "
"run them on the GPU using our custom utilities. These are used to test the "
"majority of functional implementations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:23
msgid ""
"**Integration tests** - These are lightweight tests that simply call a "
"`main` function and checks if it returns non-zero. These are primarily used "
"to test interfaces that are sensitive to threading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:27
msgid ""
"The GPU uses the same testing infrastructure as the other supported `libc` "
"targets. We do this by treating the GPU as a standard hosted environment "
"capable of launching a `main` function. Effectively, this means building our "
"own startup libraries and loader."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:32
msgid "Testing utilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:34
msgid ""
"We provide two utilities to execute arbitrary programs on the GPU. That is "
"the `loader` and the `start` object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:37
msgid "Startup object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:39
msgid ""
"This object mimics the standard object used by existing C library "
"implementations. Its job is to perform the necessary setup prior to calling "
"the `main` function. In the GPU case, this means exporting GPU kernels that "
"will perform the necessary operations. Here we use `_begin` and `_end` to "
"handle calling global constructors and destructors while `_start` begins the "
"standard execution. The following code block shows the implementation for "
"AMDGPU architectures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:65
msgid "Loader runtime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:67
msgid ""
"The startup object provides a GPU executable with callable kernels for the "
"respective runtime. We can then define a minimal runtime that will launch "
"these kernels on the given device. Currently we provide the `amdhsa-loader` "
"and `nvptx-loader` targeting the AMD HSA runtime and CUDA driver runtime "
"respectively. By default these will launch with a single thread on the GPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:79
msgid ""
"The loader utility will forward any arguments passed after the executable "
"image to the program on the GPU as well as any set environment variables. "
"The number of threads and blocks to be set can be controlled with `--"
"threads` and `--blocks`. These also accept additional `x`, `y`, `z` variants "
"for multidimensional grids."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:85
msgid "Running tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:87
msgid ""
"Tests will only be built and run if a GPU target architecture is set and the "
"corresponding loader utility was built. These can be overridden with the "
"`LIBC_GPU_TEST_ARCHITECTURE` and `CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR` {ref}`CMake "
"options <gpu_cmake_options>`. Once built, they can be run like any other "
"tests. The CMake target depends on how the library was built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:93
msgid ""
"**Cross build** - If the C library was built using `LLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS` or "
"a runtimes cross build, then the standard targets will be present in the "
"base CMake build directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:97 ../../../gpu/testing.md:118
msgid "All tests - You can run all supported tests with the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:103
msgid "Libc tests - You can run libc tests with the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:109
msgid "Integration tests - You can run integration tests by the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:115
msgid ""
"**Runtimes build** - If the library was built using `LLVM_ENABLE_RUNTIMES` "
"then the actual `libc` build will be in a separate directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:125
msgid ""
"Specific tests - You can use the same targets as above by entering the "
"runtimes build directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/testing.md:135
msgid ""
"Tests can also be built and run manually using the respective loader utility."
msgstr ""
